# How fast have measles deaths fallen since 1980?
subtitle: "Draw how measles deaths changed after 1985, then see the fall of about 90 percent, what drove it, and why the line turned up again."
tags: ["health","epidemiology","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Draw the line\" note \"1980 to now\""

## How fast have measles deaths fallen since 1980?
use: line_chart
with:
    x:
      - 1980
      - 1985
      - 1990
      - 1995
      - 2000
      - 2005
      - 2010
      - 2015
      - 2019
      - 2021
      - 2023
    series:
      - {name: Measles, values: [1386, 1290, 1103, 955, 763, 461, 285, 173, 127, 71, 144]}
      - {name: ​, values: [1386, 1290, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null]}
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 1500
    xlim:
      - 1980
      - 2023
    y_label: Deaths a year (thousands)
    points: true
    x_ticks: false
    label_size: 30
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Deaths due to measles
      authors: Our World in Data, from IHME Global Burden of Disease (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/deaths-due-to-measles-gbd
      finding: 'IHME estimates: world measles deaths about 1.39 million in 1980, 763,000 in 2000, 127,000 in 2019, 71,000 in 2021 and 144,000 in 2023 (WHO''s often-quoted figure for the pre-vaccination era is higher, about 2.6 million a year)'
    - id: owid_vax
      title: Measles vaccines save millions of lives each year
      authors: Saloni Dattani and Fiona Spooner (Our World in Data)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/measles-vaccines-save-lives
      finding: measles vaccines have saved about 94 million lives in the last 50 years; over 80 percent of infants are now vaccinated, against very low coverage in the 1980s
    - id: gbd
      title: Global Burden of Disease Study 2023
      authors: Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME)
      year: 2025
      finding: annual deaths from measles by country and year, 1980–2023 (model estimates; lower than WHO's estimates for the early years)

    dot startpt #b5482e at.data [1980,1386] hidden true
    text start "1980: 1.4 M" right startpt gap 40 #b5482e cites ["owid"] font_size 44 hidden true
    dot endpt #b5482e at.data [2023,144] hidden true
    text end "144,000" above endpt gap 45 #b5482e cites ["owid"] font_size 44 hidden true
    text drop "−90%" #b5482e at.gap 20 at.ref end at.side above cites ["owid"] font_size 64 hidden true
    icon syr size 130 set twemoji x 800 y 560 icon_look picture of syringe hidden true
    text vax "8 in 10 babies" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_vax"] x 800 y 460 font_size 44 hidden true
    text saved "94 M lives saved" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_vax"] x 800 y 460 font_size 44 hidden true
    dot lowpt #2f6b8f at.data [2021,71] hidden true
    text low "71,000" #2f6b8f at.data [2011,80] cites ["owid"] font_size 40 hidden true
    arrow rise lowpt -> endpt #b5482e style.stroke_width 7 hidden true
    text twice "about ×2" #b5482e at.gap 20 at.ref end at.side above cites ["owid"] font_size 56 hidden true
    text slip "missed shots" #b5482e x 800 y 460 font_size 44 hidden true
    path lowlead dashed #2f6b8f points [[2015.2,80],[2020.5,72]] data true style.stroke_width 2 hidden true

    card title "Where did measles deaths go?"

How many people die of measles each year, and how has that changed since 1980? By one major estimate, in 1980 it killed about one point four million, most of them small children.
    draw axes line_2 startpt start

    ask "Draw the line on from 1985 to 2023." on line_1 from 1985 store g tolerance 0.08
        default: 1250,1200,1150,1100,1050,1000,950,900,880
        intro: Five years later, it was still almost one point three million.
        right: Good line. Deaths fell, and kept on falling.
        wrong: The real fall was steep, and it lasted for decades.

By 2023, about a hundred and forty-four thousand people died of measles: around ninety percent fewer than in 1980.
    draw endpt end drop

    erase drop start

The reason is a vaccine. In the early 1980s few children got it; today more than eight in ten babies do.
    draw syr vax

    erase vax

Over fifty years, measles  (@draw saved@)vaccines have saved an estimated ninety-four million lives.

    erase saved

But look at the very end of the line. In 2021, deaths had fallen to about seventy-one thousand.
    draw lowpt low lowlead

Two years later, by this estimate, they had roughly doubled.
    draw rise twice

During the pandemic, vaccination slipped in many countries, and measles, one of the most contagious diseases there is, found the gaps.
    draw slip

So the fall only lasts while the vaccinations keep up.
    highlight rise twice

